    <tags>proxy proxies proxy-list free-proxy socks5 socks4 http https cli</tags>
    <summary>Command-line client for a free proxy list re-validated every 30 minutes</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[`proxmint` prints proxies from the Proxmint free proxy list. Every entry was checked with a real request through it within the last 30 minutes, and dead ones are dropped. No API key or signup.

## Usage

```
proxmint                          # 20 best, ip:port, one per line
proxmint -p socks5 -c de -n 50    # 50 German SOCKS5 proxies
proxmint --sort latency --url     # protocol://ip:port
proxmint --json                   # full rows as JSON
```

| Option | |
|---|---|
| `-p, --protocol` | `http`, `https`, `socks4`, `socks5` |
| `-c, --country` | ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code, e.g. `de` |
| `-a, --anonymity` | `elite`, `anonymous`, `transparent` |
| `-s, --sort` | `score`, `latency`, `uptime`, `checked` (default `score`) |
| `-n, --limit` | how many to print (default 20) |
| `--url` | print `protocol://ip:port` |
| `--json` | full rows as JSON |

Proxies go to stdout, one per line; messages and errors go to stderr. The public API allows 60 requests a minute per IP.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/proxmint/free-proxy-list/commits/main/client</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="nodejs-lts" version="20.0.0" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
